s8-5-p30 : Block
s8-5-p30 = prose (cons "A source-language memory state usually contains more than bytes: allocation identities, extents, lifetimes, permissions, pointer provenance, active union members, and synchronization events as required by that language. An address-only model is a useful target or abstract model when a theorem or explicit assumption connects it to the richer one. Reusing the same physical address after deallocation does not by itself resurrect an old source pointer." nil)
